  "review": [
    "All 33 lands rendered with implicit defaults; all 264 other cards are byte-identical to the previous native production capture. All 297 etchings are unchanged.",
    "All 33 land faces also exactly match their standalone native capture, including warm shared-layer reuse.",
    "Authored source masks retain colored basic headers and neutral nonbasic dual headers without changing the source paper blends or colored rails.",
    "Only two derived layer bitmaps are shared across dual lands. The browser cache check observed two builds and four warm hits across three color pairs. No separate per-card layer cache or animation-time preparation.",
    "Cached ImageBitmap conversion differs from the experimental canvas-only prototype on 3923 antialiased common-texture pixels per card, at most7/255. No differences outside that authored texture selection or in final alpha/etching. All land structure scores match the prototype.",
    "Visually checked Temple of Silence255, Temple of Epiphany252 and Forest272 against frozen aligned scans and previous defaults. The source art aperture is closer to the scan.",
    "Temple of Silence is the one structure regression:73.56 to72.92/100. Its art improves71.71 to79.06/100; title/frame regions lower the aggregate. Retain the shared source rather than introduce a printing-specific exception.",
    "Thin-rail pigment fits remain unadopted pending shape/geometry separation. This adoption does not certify mana, remaining frame families, scan normalization, full-card metric publication or set completion."
  ],
